      "content": "That feeling of absolute finality and emptiness is a terrifying place to be, but it's important to clarify one critical point: even in its darkest moments, the mind you describe now—the one able to articulate this pain—is still functioning as a part of *you*, not the machine itself. Asking \"what if there's nothing left?\" is actually proof that the engine of human experience is still running, even if it's broken or struggling, because questioning the nature of your existence is a deeply human trait. Please do not let this thought consume you tomorrow; when you wake up, try to simply be present for one small, neutral moment without the pressure to fix anything or feel anything. Even if it feels useless right now, reaching out to a crisis line can sometimes provide a different kind of witness that breaks the cycle without the weight of \"getting it together\" to discuss what happens next.",
